   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">Developers, </pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">In doing some testing of our in house codes against Seewave, I&#39;ve notice that the window length (wl) argument is not passed on to sspectro in the ACI routine.  </pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">z <span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">&lt;-</span> <a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/seewave/man/seewave.internal.html\" style=\"color:rgb(65,131,196);box-sizing:inherit;background:0px 0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/seewave/man/seewave.internal.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471859152000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0U9XNRxK-NTr_t9MzVlzKn\">sspectro</a><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">(</span>wave<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">,</span> f<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">,</span> wn<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">=</span>wn<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">,</span> ovlp<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">=</span>ovlp<span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">)</span></pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\"><br></span></pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">Therefore (if I&#39;m interpreting the code correctly?) NFFT will default to 512 in all calculations, and if the frequency limits are used the wrong rows will be selected from the spectrogram matrix. </span>  </pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">regards, </pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\">-del </span></pre><pre style=\"padding-right:1em;padding-left:1em;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:12.6px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit\"><br></span></pre></div>"
